<p>
Gracious Father,
</p>

<p>
Holy Saturday,<br>
the day of waiting,<br>
after all of our<br>
hopes and dreams<br>
have been crushed<br>
by a cruel world<br>
and a naive idealism<br>
is forced to succumb<br>
to a harsher reality.
</p>

<p>
But even after the<br>
horrors of Friday,<br>
the morning sun still<br>
rose on Saturday.
</p>

<p>
And we have hope,<br>
however faint,<br>
however absurd.
</p>

<p>
So we wait,<br>
wait to see<br>
what Sunday<br>
will bring.
</p>

<p>
Amen
</p>


